WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.120
Here's how to bring a driving game's telemetry into PadForge,

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.450
and buzz the trigger at the redline.

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.710
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:13.295
On the Dashboard, tick Listen for Game Telemetry.

5
00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:15.385
Leave the game on Auto-Detect,

6
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:19.355
and point the game's telemetry output at this PC and this port.

7
00:00:20.864 --> 00:00:25.674
The Devices page now lists a Game Telemetry row: speed, RPM,

8
00:00:26.384 --> 00:00:29.334
pedals, steering and gear, ready to map like a controller.

9
00:00:31.957 --> 00:00:35.587
For a redline buzz, open the controller's Macros tab,

10
00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:38.687
add a macro, and set Fire to Custom Expression.

11
00:00:41.057 --> 00:00:42.267
Add a variable.

12
00:00:42.677 --> 00:00:47.207
Set its source to Game Telemetry, and pick RPM, as a percent of the maximum.

13
00:00:48.582 --> 00:00:51.372
In the formula, type a > 95.

14
00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:56.649
Then add an action.

15
00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.669
Make it an Adaptive Trigger Effect on the right trigger, and pick Vibration.

16
00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:07.249
With a game sending, the trigger buzzes above 95 percent RPM.

17
00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:08.659
No game ran for this video.

18
00:01:11.075 --> 00:01:13.605
Find more guides at padforge.org.
